<title>USA: Two U.S. senators to visit Bosnia, Serbia.</title>
<headline>Two U.S. senators to visit Bosnia, Serbia.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two Democratic senators left on Friday to visit U.S. troops and NATO officials in Bosnia, Serbia and Croatia.</p>
<p>&quot;I want to see firsthand how our troops are doing while they are serving in a difficult and dangerous part of the world,&quot; Jack Reed of Rhode Island said in a statement.</p>
<p>Reed, a former Army officer who was sworn in as a senator on Tuesday after six years in the U.S. House of Representatives, was joined on the trip by Carl Levin of Michigan, the senior Democrat on the Senate Armed Services Committee.</p>
